#: src/overview.md:16
msgid ""
"_Table 1. Four journal entries of a small shop. The debit total and the "
"credit total are both 3,000._"
msgstr ""
"_表 1. 小さな店舗の 4 件の仕訳. 借方合計と貸方合計はともに 3,000 です._"

#: src/overview.md:18
msgid "The same journal in exchange algebra"
msgstr "同じ仕訳帳を交換代数で表す"

#: src/overview.md:20
msgid ""
"Exchange algebra writes an entry as a sum of terms $a : e$, where $a$ is a "
"nonnegative amount and $e$ is a base. Here a base is an account title in "
"angle brackets. A base with `Not`, such as $\\langle \\text{Cash} \\rangle$, "
"records an increase. A base with `Hat`, such as $\\widehat{\\langle "
"\\text{Cash} \\rangle}$, records a decrease. The four rows of Table 1 become:"
msgstr ""
"交換代数では, 仕訳を項 $a : e$ の和で表します. $a$ は非負の金額, $e$ は基底で"
"す. ここでは, 山括弧で囲んだ勘定科目が基底に当たります. $\\langle "
"\\text{Cash} \\rangle$ のように `Not` の付いた基底は増加を表します. $"
"\\widehat{\\langle \\text{Cash} \\rangle}$ のように `Hat` の付いた基底は減少"
"を表します. 表 1 の 4 行は次のようになります:"

#: src/overview.md:22
msgid ""
"$$ \\\\begin{aligned} x_1 &= 1000 : \\langle \\text{Cash} \\rangle + 1000 : "
"\\langle \\text{Capital stock} \\rangle \\\\\\\\ x_2 &= 600 : \\langle "
"\\text{Purchases} \\rangle + 600 : \\widehat{\\langle \\text{Cash} \\rangle} "
"\\\\\\\\ x_3 &= 900 : \\langle \\text{Accounts receivable} \\rangle + 900 : "
"\\langle \\text{Sales} \\rangle \\\\\\\\ x_4 &= 500 : \\langle \\text{Cash} "
"\\rangle + 500 : \\widehat{\\langle \\text{Accounts receivable} \\rangle} \\"
"\\end{aligned} $$"
msgstr ""
"$$ \\\\begin{aligned} x_1 &= 1000 : \\langle \\text{Cash} \\rangle + 1000 : "
"\\langle \\text{Capital stock} \\rangle \\\\\\\\ x_2 &= 600 : \\langle "
"\\text{Purchases} \\rangle + 600 : \\widehat{\\langle \\text{Cash} \\rangle} "
"\\\\\\\\ x_3 &= 900 : \\langle \\text{Accounts receivable} \\rangle + 900 : "
"\\langle \\text{Sales} \\rangle \\\\\\\\ x_4 &= 500 : \\langle \\text{Cash} "
"\\rangle + 500 : \\widehat{\\langle \\text{Accounts receivable} \\rangle} \\"
"\\end{aligned} $$"

#: src/overview.md:31
msgid ""
"The terms carry neither debit and credit labels nor minus signs. Each term "
"states which account changed and in which direction. The journal side "
"follows from the account's division: an increase in an asset or expense is a "
"debit, and an increase in a liability, equity, or revenue account is a "
"credit. A decrease takes the opposite side. For example, the increase in "
"capital stock in $x_1$ is a credit, and the decrease in cash in $x_2$ is "
"also a credit. [Account classes and sides](algebra/definitions.md#account-"
"classes-and-sides) gives the full rule, including contra accounts."
msgstr ""
"項には借方や貸方のラベルも負号も付けません. 各項は, どの勘定がどちらの方向に"
"変化したかを表します. 借方と貸方の別は勘定の区分から決まります. 資産と費用の"
"増加は借方, 負債, 純資産, 収益の増加は貸方です. 減少の場合は反対側になりま"
"す. 例えば, $x_1$ の資本金の増加も, $x_2$ の現金の減少も貸方です. 評価勘定を"
"含む規則の全体は[勘定の区分と貸借](algebra/definitions.md#account-classes-"
"and-sides)を参照してください."

#: src/overview.md:33
msgid ""
"The combined record is the sum $x = x_1 + x_2 + x_3 + x_4$ of eight terms. "
"The sum keeps every term: cash has $1000$ and $500$ on the base with `Not` "
"and $600$ on the base with `Hat`. Bar, written $\\bar{x}$, totals the two "
"directions at each base and keeps the excess. For cash it leaves $900 : "
"\\langle \\text{Cash} \\rangle$, the cash balance."
msgstr ""
"記録全体を合わせると, 8 個の項の和 $x = x_1 + x_2 + x_3 + x_4$ です. 和はすべ"
"ての項を保持します. 現金については, `Not` の付いた基底に $1000$ と $500$, "
"`Hat` の付いた基底に $600$ が記録されます. $\\bar{x}$ と書く bar は, 各基底の"
"両方向をそれぞれ合計し, 差額を残します. 現金では $900 : \\langle "
"\\text{Cash} \\rangle$ が残り, 現金残高を表します."

#: src/overview.md:35
msgid "Recover the debit and credit columns"
msgstr "借方列と貸方列を取り出す"

#: src/overview.md:37
msgid ""
"The projection `decL` selects the debit terms of $x$ and `decR` selects the "
"credit terms. `decL` returns cash 1,000, purchases 600, accounts receivable "
"900, and cash 500, which is the debit column of Table 1. `decR` returns the "
"credit column. Both totals are 3,000, so `balance` returns `True`."
msgstr ""
"射影 `decL` は $x$ の借方の項を, `decR` は貸方の項を選びます. `decL` が返すの"
"は現金 1,000, 仕入 600, 売掛金 900, 現金 500 で, 表 1 の借方列に一致します. "
"`decR` は貸方列を返します. 両方の合計が 3,000 なので, `balance` は `True` を"
"返します."

#: src/overview.md:39
msgid ""
"A program that builds the journal of Table 1 and checks these results needs "
"only the `ExchangeAlgebra` module:"
msgstr ""
"表 1 の仕訳帳を構築してこれらの結果を確かめるプログラムは, `ExchangeAlgebra` "
"モジュールだけで書けます:"

#: src/overview.md:57
msgid "It prints:"
msgstr "出力は次のとおりです:"

#: src/overview.md:65
msgid ""
"`.@` attaches an amount to a hat base. `.+` keeps the terms of both "
"operands, including terms on the same base. `norm` totals the amounts. `bar` "
"offsets the increases and decreases of the cash terms selected by "
"`projByAccountTitle` and leaves the net increase of 900."
msgstr ""
"`.@` は金額を Hat 基底に付けます. `.+` は, 同じ基底の項も含めて両方の被演算子"
"の項を保持します. `norm` は金額を合計します. `bar` は, `projByAccountTitle` "
"で選んだ現金の項の増加と減少を相殺し, 正味の増加 900 を残します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:3
msgid ""
"**Note:** The mathematical definitions are optional background for using the "
"library. If you prefer to skip the mathematics, go to [Installation and "
"modules](../usage/installation.md)."
msgstr ""
"**補足:** 数学的な定義は, ライブラリを使ううえで必須の知識ではありません. 数"
"学の説明を読み飛ばす場合は, [導入とモジュール](../usage/installation.md)へ進"
"んでください."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:5
msgid "Element structure"
msgstr "要素構造"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:7
msgid ""
"**Definition 1 (Element structure).** Each element set $E$ has a "
"distinguished wildcard element $\\\\# \\in E$ and a total order $\\leq$. For "
"a query element $p$ and a stored element $e$ in $E$, one-way matching is "
"defined by"
msgstr ""
"**定義 1 (要素構造).** 各要素集合 $E$ には, 特別なワイルドカード要素 $\\\\# "
"\\in E$ と全順序 $\\leq$ があります. $E$ に属する問い合わせの要素 $p$ と記録"
"された要素 $e$ の片方向の照合を, 次の式で定義します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:9
msgid ""
"$$ p \\trianglerighteq e \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad (p=\\\\#)"
"\\lor(p=e). $$"
msgstr ""
"$$ p \\trianglerighteq e \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad (p=\\\\#)"
"\\lor(p=e). $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:13
msgid ""
"A stored $\\\\#$ indicates that the corresponding element set does not "
"apply. A query for a specific firm therefore skips a term whose firm element "
"is $\\\\#$. The wildcard is an ordinary member of the total order; matching "
"does not define that order."
msgstr ""
"記録された $\\\\#$ は, 対応する要素集合が該当しないことを表します. したがっ"
"て, 特定の企業を指定する問い合わせは, 企業の要素が $\\\\#$ である項 を選びま"
"せん. ワイルドカードは全順序集合の通常の元であり, 照合によってその順序が定ま"
"るわけではありません."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:15
msgid ""
"Definition 1 of the preprint gives a symmetric comparison. The query "
"relation used here treats only a query-side $\\\\#$ as a pattern."
msgstr ""
"プレプリントの定義 1 は対称な比較を与えています. ここで使う問い合わせの関係で"
"は, 問い合わせ側の $\\\\#$ だけをパターンとして扱います."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:17
msgid "Usage: [Elements](elements.md)."
msgstr "使い方: [要素](elements.md)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:21
msgid ""
"**Definition 2.** A base is a tuple of elements, one from each element set. "
"For element sets $E_1,\\ldots,E_n$, the base space is "
"$E_1\\times\\cdots\\times E_n$. An account and a firm, for example, form a "
"base with two elements. A query tuple matches a stored base exactly when "
"each query element matches the corresponding stored element."
msgstr ""
"**定義 2.** 基底は, 各要素集合から 1 つずつ要素を取ったタプルです. 要素集合 "
"$E_1,\\ldots,E_n$ に対して, 基底空間は $E_1\\times\\cdots\\times E_n$ です. "
"例えば, 勘定と企業は 2 つの要素を持つ基底を構成します. 問い合わせの各要素が対"
"応する記録済みの要素に一致するとき, かつそのときに限り, 問い合わせのタプルは"
"記録された基底に一致します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:23
msgid ""
"Here, “element” refers to a member of an element set that supplies a "
"component of a base, while a “member of the redundant algebra” is a sum of "
"terms."
msgstr ""
"ここでの「要素」は基底の成分を与える要素集合の元を指し, 「冗長代数の元」は項"
"の和を指します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:25
msgid "Usage: [Bases](bases.md)."
msgstr "使い方: [基底](bases.md)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:27
msgid "Hat bases and terms"
msgstr "Hat 基底と項"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:29
msgid ""
"**Definition 3.** A hat base pairs a base with one of two directions: `Not` "
"(increase) or `Hat` (decrease). A query can select both directions with "
"`HatNot`. Each term has a direction of `Not` or `Hat`."
msgstr ""
"**定義 3.** Hat 基底は, 基底と 2 つの方向のいずれかを組にしたものです. 方向"
"は `Not` (増加) または `Hat` (減少) です. 問い合わせでは `HatNot` で両方向を"
"選択できます. 各項の方向は `Not` または `Hat` です."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:31
msgid ""
"A term pairs a hat base with a nonnegative real amount from the value domain "
"$V\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}\\_{\\geq 0}$. We write $a:e$ for an increase and $a:"
"\\widehat{e}$ for a decrease at the base $e$. The redundant algebra is "
"generated by its terms. In Haskell, `Posting` is the type that represents a "
"term."
msgstr ""
"項は, Hat 基底と値域 $V\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}\\_{\\geq 0}$ の非負実数の金額を"
"組にしたものです. 基底 $e$ での増加を $a:e$, 減少を $a:\\widehat{e}$ と書きま"
"す. 項は冗長代数の生成元です. Haskell では `Posting` が項を表す型です."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:33
msgid "Usage: [Bases](bases.md) and [Values](values.md)."
msgstr "使い方: [基底](bases.md)と[値](values.md)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:35
msgid "Redundant algebra and linear combinations"
msgstr "冗長代数と線形結合"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:37
msgid ""
"**Definition 4.** A redundant algebra consists of finite collections of "
"terms, with addition, scalar multiplication by nonnegative values, hat, bar, "
"and a norm into the value domain."
msgstr ""
"**定義 4.** 冗長代数は項の有限な集まりからなり, 加法, 非負の値によるスカラー"
"倍, hat, bar, 値域への norm を備えます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:39
msgid "Usage: [The redundant algebra](redundant.md) and [Values](values.md)."
msgstr "使い方: [冗長代数](redundant.md)と[値](values.md)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:41
msgid ""
"**Definition 5.** At each underlying base $e_i$, a member of the redundant "
"algebra records two finite sequences of amounts. Write $f_i(e_i)=\\langle "
"A_i,B_i\\rangle$, with $A_i$ the increase sequence and $B_i$ the decrease "
"sequence. Two increases of 3 and 2 at the same base remain separate terms "
"until an operation explicitly combines them. A member of the redundant "
"algebra $x=\\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle$ has finite support over the "
"bases. An empty sequence pair contributes zero."
msgstr ""
"**定義 5.** 各基底 $e_i$ において, 冗長代数の元は金額の 2 つの有限列を記録し"
"ます. $f_i(e_i)=\\langle A_i,B_i\\rangle$ と書き, $A_i$ を増加の列, $B_i$ を"
"減少の列とします. 同じ基底での 3 と 2 の 2 つの増加は, 演算で明示的にまとめる"
"まで別々の項として残ります. 冗長代数の元 $x=\\langle "
"f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle$ は基底上で有限な台を持ちます. 空の列の対は寄与しませ"
"ん."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:43
msgid ""
"Usage: [Construct terms and add them](redundant.md#construct-postings-and-"
"add-them)."
msgstr ""
"使い方: [項を構築して加算する](redundant.md#construct-postings-and-add-them)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:45
msgid "Operations"
msgstr "演算"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:47
msgid ""
"**Definition 6.** The operations on the paired sequences are as follows."
msgstr "**定義 6.** 対になった列に対する演算は次のとおりです."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:49 src/algebra/redundant.md:155
#: src/exchange/transfer.md:121
msgid "Operation"
msgstr "演算"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:49
msgid "Effect"
msgstr "作用"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:51
msgid "Hat"
msgstr "hat"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:51
msgid "Swap the two sequences at each base, preserving every amount."
msgstr "各基底の 2 つの列を入れ替え, すべての金額を保持します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:52
msgid "Bar"
msgstr "bar"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:52
msgid ""
"Total each sequence at each base and cancel the two totals. Keep the excess "
"on the larger side and drop a zero remainder."
msgstr ""
"各基底でそれぞれの列を合計し, 2 つの合計を相殺します. 大きい側に差額を残し, "
"残額がゼロなら取り除きます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:53
msgid "Sum"
msgstr "和"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:53
msgid "Concatenate the corresponding sequences."
msgstr "対応する列を連結します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:54
msgid "Scalar multiplication"
msgstr "スカラー倍"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:54
msgid "Multiply every amount by the same nonnegative scalar."
msgstr "すべての金額に同じ非負のスカラーを掛けます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:55
msgid "Norm"
msgstr "norm"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:55
msgid "Sum all amounts on both sides over all bases."
msgstr "すべての基底にわたって両側の全金額を合計します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:57
msgid ""
"The library adds `compress`, which sums amounts separately for each base and "
"each direction (`Hat` or `Not`)."
msgstr ""
"ライブラリが追加した演算 `compress` は, 基底と方向 (`Hat` または `Not`) ごと"
"に金額を合算します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:59
msgid ""
"For bar, write $\\[z\\]\\_+=\\max(0,z)$. If $A_i=(a\\_{i1},"
"\\ldots,a\\_{ip_i})$ and $B_i=(b\\_{i1},\\ldots,b\\_{iq_i})$, the remaining "
"increase and decrease are"
msgstr ""
"bar について, $\\[z\\]\\_+=\\max(0,z)$ と書きます. $A_i=(a\\_{i1},"
"\\ldots,a\\_{ip_i})$, $B_i=(b\\_{i1},\\ldots,b\\_{iq_i})$ のとき, 残る増加と"
"減少は次のとおりです:"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:61
msgid ""
"$$ D_i=\\left\\[\\\\sum_j a\\_{ij}-\\sum_k b\\_{ik}\\right\\]\\_+, \\\\qquad "
"R_i=\\left\\[\\\\sum_k b\\_{ik}-\\sum_j a\\_{ij}\\right\\]\\_+. $$"
msgstr ""
"$$ D_i=\\left\\[\\\\sum_j a\\_{ij}-\\sum_k b\\_{ik}\\right\\]\\_+, \\\\qquad "
"R_i=\\left\\[\\\\sum_k b\\_{ik}-\\sum_j a\\_{ij}\\right\\]\\_+. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:67
msgid ""
"For example, two increases of 3 and 2 and a decrease of 4 on the same base "
"have norm 9. Applying `compress` gives an increase of 5 and a decrease of 4. "
"Bar leaves an increase of 1. In general, the contribution to the norm is"
msgstr ""
"例えば, 同じ基底での 3 と 2 の 2 つの増加と 4 の減少の norm は 9 です. "
"`compress` を適用すると, 5 の増加と 4 の減少になります. bar を適用すると 1 の"
"増加が残ります. 一般に, norm への寄与は次のとおりです:"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:69
msgid ""
"$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)) = \\sum\\_{j=1}^{p_i} a\\_{ij} + "
"\\sum\\_{k=1}^{q_i} b\\_{ik}. $$"
msgstr ""
"$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)) = \\sum\\_{j=1}^{p_i} a\\_{ij} + "
"\\sum\\_{k=1}^{q_i} b\\_{ik}. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:73
msgid "Usage: [Select an operation](redundant.md#select-an-operation)."
msgstr "使い方: [演算を選ぶ](redundant.md#select-an-operation)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:75
msgid "Five axioms"
msgstr "5 つの公理"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:77
msgid ""
"Let $x=\\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle$ and let $a$ be a nonnegative scalar."
msgstr "$x=\\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle$ とし, $a$ を非負スカラーとします."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:79
msgid ""
"**Hat is an involution.** Applying hat twice restores the original terms."
msgstr "**hat の対合性.** hat を 2 回適用すると元の項に戻ります."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:81
msgid "$$ \\\\widehat{\\widehat{f_i}}(e_i) = f_i(e_i). $$"
msgstr "$$ \\\\widehat{\\widehat{f_i}}(e_i) = f_i(e_i). $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:85
msgid ""
"**Scaling at one base.** The scalar acts on each amount in each sequence."
msgstr "**1 つの基底でのスカラー倍.** スカラーは各列の各金額に作用します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:87
msgid "$$ a \\ast f_i(e_i) = \\langle a \\ast A_i, a \\ast B_i\\rangle. $$"
msgstr "$$ a \\ast f_i(e_i) = \\langle a \\ast A_i, a \\ast B_i\\rangle. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:91
msgid "**Scaling across bases.** The scalar acts on every component."
msgstr "**基底全体のスカラー倍.** スカラーはすべての成分に作用します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:93
msgid ""
"$$ a \\ast \\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle = \\langle a \\ast f_1,\\ldots,a "
"\\ast f_n\\rangle. $$"
msgstr ""
"$$ a \\ast \\langle f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\rangle = \\langle a \\ast f_1,\\ldots,a "
"\\ast f_n\\rangle. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:97
msgid "**Norm homogeneity.** Scaling the terms scales their total."
msgstr ""
"**norm の斉次性.** 項をスカラー倍すると, 合計も同じスカラー倍になります."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:99
msgid ""
"$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(a \\ast x) = a \\cdot \\operatorname{norm}(x), "
"\\qquad a \\ge 0. $$"
msgstr ""
"$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(a \\ast x) = a \\cdot \\operatorname{norm}(x), "
"\\qquad a \\ge 0. $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:103
msgid "**Norm additivity.** Adding terms adds their totals."
msgstr "**norm の加法性.** 項を加えると, それぞれの合計も加わります."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:105
msgid ""
"$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)+g_i(e_i)) = \\operatorname{norm}"
"(f_i(e_i)) + \\operatorname{norm}(g_i(e_i)). $$"
msgstr ""
"$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(f_i(e_i)+g_i(e_i)) = \\operatorname{norm}"
"(f_i(e_i)) + \\operatorname{norm}(g_i(e_i)). $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:109
msgid ""
"The preprint lists the defining sum of the norm under the name “norm "
"homogeneity.” The homogeneity law above follows from that sum and the scalar "
"multiplication."
msgstr ""
"プレプリントでは, norm を定義する和を「norm の斉次性」という名称で挙げていま"
"す. ここに示した斉次性の法則は, その和とスカラー倍から導かれます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:111
msgid ""
"Axioms 4 and 5 hold exactly with exact decimal arithmetic when the amounts, "
"intermediate sums, and products are representable. With binary floating-"
"point arithmetic, summing stored amounts exactly and rounding once still "
"permits the two sides to differ in the last digit: scaling can round "
"individual products, and adding two norms can use two already rounded totals."
msgstr ""
"金額と中間の和および積を表現できるとき, 正確な十進演算では公理 4 と 5 が厳密"
"に成立します. 二進浮動小数点演算では, 記録された金額を厳密に合計して最後に 1 "
"回だけ丸めても, 両辺の末尾の桁が異なることがあります. スカラー倍では個々の積"
"が丸められ, 2 つの norm の加算では既に丸められた 2 つの合計を使うことがあるた"
"めです."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:113
msgid ""
"Usage: [Values and the numerical conditions](values.md#choose-an-amount-"
"type)."
msgstr "使い方: [値と数値的条件](values.md#choose-an-amount-type)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:115
msgid "Account classes and sides"
msgstr "勘定の区分と貸借"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:117
msgid ""
"**Definition 7.** An exchange base carries an account title with an account "
"division and a home side. Its debit or credit side combines that home side "
"with the direction. In the library, `whatPIMO` classifies the account as "
"plus stock, inflow, minus stock, or outflow, and `fixedCurrent` classifies "
"it as current, fixed, or other. For ordinary accounts the assignment is:"
msgstr ""
"**定義 7.** 交換基底は, 勘定区分と本来の貸借の側を持つ勘定科目を含みます. 項"
"の貸借の側は, その本来の側と方向を組み合わせて決まります. ライブラリでは, "
"`whatPIMO` は勘定をストック増加・流入・ストック減少・流出に分類し, "
"`fixedCurrent` は流動・固定・その他に分類します. 通常の勘定の対応は次のとおり"
"です."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:119 src/usage/withdrawal.md:89
msgid "Division"
msgstr "区分"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:119
msgid "Increase"
msgstr "増加"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:119
msgid "Decrease"
msgstr "減少"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:121
msgid "Assets, expenses (costs)"
msgstr "資産, 費用 (原価)"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:122
msgid "Liabilities, equity, revenue"
msgstr "負債, 純資産, 収益"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:124
msgid ""
"A contra account reverses the home side of its division before the direction "
"is applied."
msgstr ""
"評価勘定では, 方向を適用する前に, その区分が本来持つ貸借の側を反転します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:126
msgid ""
"Usage: [The journal example](../overview.md#the-same-journal-in-exchange-"
"algebra)."
msgstr ""
"使い方: [仕訳帳の例](../overview.md#the-same-journal-in-exchange-algebra)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:128
msgid "Debit and credit decomposition"
msgstr "借方と貸方への分解"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:130
msgid ""
"**Definition 8.** An exchange algebra extends the redundant algebra with "
"four decompositions. `decL` selects debit terms (left), and `decR` selects "
"credit terms (right). The other two decompositions select by direction. "
"`decP` selects terms with `Hat`, and `decM` selects terms with `Not`. For "
"example, a decrease in cash is a credit, and an increase in an ordinary "
"expense is a debit. A sum of terms is balanced when its exact debit and "
"credit totals agree."
msgstr ""
"**定義 8.** 交換代数は, 冗長代数に 4 つの分解の演算を加えたものです. `decL` "
"は借方 (左側) の項を, `decR` は貸方 (右側) の項を選びます. 残る 2 つの演算は"
"方向で分解します. `decP` は `Hat` の付いた項を, `decM` は `Not` の付いた項を"
"選びます. 例えば, 現金の減少は貸方であり, 通常の費用の増加は借方です. 項の和"
"の借方合計と貸方合計が厳密に等しいとき, 貸借が一致します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:132
msgid ""
"Usage: [Recover the debit and credit columns](../overview.md#recover-the-"
"debit-and-credit-columns)."
msgstr ""
"使い方: [借方列と貸方列を取り出す](../overview.md#recover-the-debit-and-"
"credit-columns)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:136
msgid ""
"**Definition 9.** A transfer table is an ordered collection of triples $"
"(b_i,a_i,f_i)$, where $b_i$ is a source base, $a_i$ is a destination base, "
"and $f_i:V\\to V$ transforms a nonnegative amount. Applying the table moves "
"the selected amounts from their source bases to their destination bases "
"according to those transformations. The source base, destination base, and "
"value transformation are separate parts of each rule."
msgstr ""
"**定義 9.** 振替表は三つ組 $(b_i,a_i,f_i)$ を順序付きで集めたものです. $b_i$ "
"は振替元の基底, $a_i$ は振替先の基底で, $f_i:V\\to V$ は非負の額を変換しま"
"す. 表を適用すると, 選択した額が変換に従って振替元から振替先へ移ります. 各規"
"則では, 振替元の基底, 振替先の基底, 値の変換を別々に指定します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:138
msgid ""
"A source wildcard matches any stored element. A destination wildcard retains "
"the corresponding source element. For an accounting reclassification, the "
"amount removed from the source equals the amount added at the destination."
msgstr ""
"振替元のワイルドカードは格納された任意の要素に一致します. 振替先のワイルド"
"カードは対応する振替元の要素を保ちます. 会計上の付け替えでは, 振替元から取り"
"除く額と振替先へ加える額が等しくなります."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:140
msgid ""
"The rules of the algebra layer are sorted by source pattern, as in the "
"preprint. The accounting transfer table preserves written row order and "
"permits a destination to match a later source, but rejects a match with the "
"source of the same or an earlier row; see [Transfers](../exchange/"
"transfer.md)."
msgstr ""
"代数層の規則は, プレプリントと同じく振替元のパターン順に並べられます. 会計の"
"振替表は記述した行順を保ち, 振替先が後の行の振替元に一致する場合は受け入れま"
"すが, 同じ行または前の行の振替元に一致する場合は拒否します. 詳しくは[振替]"
"(../exchange/transfer.md)を参照してください."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:142
msgid "Usage: [Transfers](../exchange/transfer.md)."
msgstr "使い方: [振替](../exchange/transfer.md)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:144
msgid "Notes"
msgstr "摘要"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:146
msgid ""
"**Definition 10.** A note set $N$ is a totally ordered set with equality and "
"a distinguished empty element $\\mathrm{plank}\\in N$. A note can contain a "
"date, a description, or a transaction identifier."
msgstr ""
"**定義 10.** 摘要 (note) の集合 $N$ は, 等値比較と特別な空要素 $"
"\\mathrm{plank}\\in N$ を備えた全順序集合です. 摘要には日付, 説明, 取引識別子"
"などを含められます."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:148
msgid ""
"Usage: [Declare a note type](../journal/journal.md#declare-a-note-type)."
msgstr ""
"使い方: [摘要の型を宣言する](../journal/journal.md#declare-a-note-type)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:150
msgid "Finite journals"
msgstr "有限台を持つ仕訳帳"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:152
msgid ""
"**Definition 11.** A journal is a finite-support function $J:N\\to E$, where "
"$E$ is the exchange algebra. A note outside the support has value zero. "
"Equivalently, the journal is the finite collection of its nonzero note-"
"algebra pairs $(n,J(n))$. Equal notes identify the same algebra component."
msgstr ""
"**定義 11.** 仕訳帳は有限台を持つ関数 $J:N\\to E$ です. $E$ は交換代数です. "
"台に含まれない摘要では値をゼロとします. 同じ仕訳帳は, ゼロでない摘要と代数の"
"対 $(n,J(n))$ を有限個集めたものとしても表せます. 等しい摘要は同じ代数成分を"
"指します."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:154
msgid ""
"Usage: [Attach notes to the month](../journal/journal.md#attach-notes-to-the-"
"month)."
msgstr ""
"使い方: [月の取引に摘要を付ける](../journal/journal.md#attach-notes-to-the-"
"month)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:156
msgid "Journal operations"
msgstr "仕訳帳の演算"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:158
msgid ""
"**Definition 12.** Hat and scalar multiplication act separately on each "
"note's algebra, preserving its note. Addition combines the algebras at each "
"equal note by redundant addition:"
msgstr ""
"**定義 12.** Hat とスカラー倍は各摘要の代数に個別に作用し, 摘要を保ちます. 加"
"算は, 等しい摘要に対応する代数を冗長加算で合わせます:"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:160
msgid "$$ (J_1+J_2)(n)=J_1(n)+J_2(n). $$"
msgstr "$$ (J_1+J_2)(n)=J_1(n)+J_2(n). $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:164
msgid ""
"Aggregation combines the note components under the empty note. Its algebra "
"is $\\sum\\_{n\\in N}J(n)$; applying bar to that combined algebra gives the "
"journal bar. The norm counts all amounts across notes:"
msgstr ""
"集約では各摘要の成分を空の摘要にまとめます. 対応する代数は $\\sum\\_{n\\in N}"
"J(n)$ です. この代数に bar を適用すると仕訳帳の bar が得られます. norm は摘要"
"をまたいで全ての額を数えます:"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:166
msgid ""
"$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(J)=\\operatorname{norm}\\left(\\sum\\_{n\\in N}J(n)"
"\\right). $$"
msgstr ""
"$$ \\\\operatorname{norm}(J)=\\operatorname{norm}\\left(\\sum\\_{n\\in N}J(n)"
"\\right). $$"

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:170
msgid ""
"A note projection selects note keys; a base projection selects terms within "
"the selected notes. A joint projection restricts both. Neither projection "
"requires aggregation or cancellation."
msgstr ""
"摘要による射影は摘要のキーを選びます. 基底による射影は選択した摘要の中から項"
"を選びます. 両方による射影は摘要と基底をともに制限します. どちらの射影にも集"
"約や相殺は必要ありません."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:172
msgid ""
"Usage: [Select by note, base, and date](../journal/journal.md#select-by-note-"
"base-and-date) and [Total amounts and combine notes](../journal/"
"journal.md#total-amounts-and-combine-notes)."
msgstr ""
"使い方: [摘要, 基底, 日付で選ぶ](../journal/journal.md#select-by-note-base-"
"and-date)と[額を合計して摘要をまとめる](../journal/journal.md#total-amounts-"
"and-combine-notes)."

#: src/algebra/definitions.md:174
msgid ""
"Definitions 1–12 follow Appendix A of [_Accounting State Space as a "
"Foundation for Economic Agent-Based Modeling: An Input–Output Benchmark and "
"Inventory Extension_](https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-8485050/v2), with the "
"query matching and norm clarification stated in Definitions 1 and 6."
msgstr ""
"定義 1–12 は [_Accounting State Space as a Foundation for Economic Agent-"
"Based Modeling: An Input–Output Benchmark and Inventory Extension_](https://"
"doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-8485050/v2) の Appendix A に従います. 問い合わせの照"
"合と norm に関する補足は定義 1 と 6 に記しています."

#: src/usage/installation.md:3
msgid ""
"This manual uses **exchangealgebra-0.6.1.1** from Hackage. The examples "
"assume that you can write Haskell programs and have Stack installed. They "
"use GHC 9.10.3 with the Stackage snapshot `lts-24.65`."
msgstr ""
"このマニュアルでは, Hackage の **exchangealgebra-0.6.1.1** を使います. 例は, "
"Haskell のプログラムを書けることと Stack の導入が済んでいることを前提としま"
"す. GHC 9.10.3 と Stackage snapshot `lts-24.65` を使います."

#: src/usage/installation.md:5
msgid ""
"The Algebra layer provides types for elements, bases, amounts, and finite "
"sequences of terms. Its operations implement the [redundant algebra](../"
"algebra/definitions.md#redundant-algebra-and-linear-combinations). "
"Accounting adds the interpretation of account titles and the debit and "
"credit sides."
msgstr ""
"Algebra 層は, 要素, 基底, 金額, 項 の有限列を表す型を提供します. その演算は"
"[冗長代数](../algebra/definitions.md#redundant-algebra-and-linear-"
"combinations)を実装します. Accounting は, 勘定科目と借方および貸方の解釈を加"
"えます."

