msgstr "\"Zero scalar times withdrawal\""

#: src/algebra/values.md:187
msgid ""
"Each rejection result names its input condition. `Negative scalar times "
"Zero` and `Zero scalar times withdrawal` report the zero shortcuts, rather "
"than rejected inputs."
msgstr ""
"拒否の結果にはそれぞれ入力条件の名前が付いています. `Negative scalar times "
"Zero` と `Zero scalar times withdrawal` は, 入力の拒否ではなくゼロによる簡約"
"を報告します."

#: src/algebra/values.md:191
msgid "HatVal methods and laws"
msgstr "HatVal のメソッドと法則"

#: src/algebra/values.md:193
msgid ""
"`HatVal` requires `Show`, `Ord`, `Eq`, `Nearly`, `Fractional`, and `Num`. "
"Built-in instances include `MoneyDecimal`, `MoneyDouble`, and bare `Double`."
msgstr ""
"`HatVal` は `Show`, `Ord`, `Eq`, `Nearly`, `Fractional`, `Num` を要求します. "
"組み込みの instance には `MoneyDecimal`, `MoneyDouble`, 単独の `Double` があ"
"ります."

#: src/algebra/values.md:195
msgid "Methods"
msgstr "メソッド"

#: src/algebra/values.md:197
msgid "`zeroValue`, `isZeroValue`"
msgstr "`zeroValue`, `isZeroValue`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:197
msgid "Define zero and test it. `isZeroValue` has an equality-based default."
msgstr ""
"ゼロを定義し, ゼロかどうかを判定します. `isZeroValue` は等値比較に基づく既定"
"の実装を持ちます."

#: src/algebra/values.md:198
msgid "`valueError`"
msgstr "`valueError`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:198
msgid ""
"Return `Nothing` for a finite nonnegative value, `Just NegativeValue` for a "
"negative finite value, or `Just NonFiniteValue` for NaN or either infinity."
msgstr ""
"有限の非負値には `Nothing`, 有限の負値には `Just NegativeValue`, NaN またはい"
"ずれかの無限大には `Just NonFiniteValue` を返します."

#: src/algebra/values.md:199
msgid "`postingUpperBound`"
msgstr "`postingUpperBound`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:199
msgid ""
"An optional bound used by checked term construction. Its default is "
"`Nothing`; the floating-point instances use a bound of 2^900."
msgstr ""
"検査付きで項を構築するときに使う, 任意の上限です. 既定値は `Nothing` です. 浮"
"動小数点の instance は 2^900 を上限に使います."

#: src/algebra/values.md:200
msgid "`showValue`"
msgstr "`showValue`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:200
msgid ""
"Render an amount inside the algebra's `Show` output. Decimal amounts retain "
"decimal formatting; floating-point amounts use the instance's formatting."
msgstr ""
"代数の `Show` 出力の中で金額を表示します. 十進数の金額は十進数の書式を保持"
"し, 浮動小数点の金額はその instance の書式を使います."

#: src/algebra/values.md:201
msgid "Associated data family `Accum n`"
msgstr "関連データ族 `Accum n`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:201
msgid ""
"Represent an exact signed sum, including special states if the value type "
"has NaN or infinities."
msgstr ""
"正確な符号付きの和を表します. 値の型が NaN または無限大を持つ場合は, その特殊"
"な状態も含みます."

#: src/algebra/values.md:202
msgid "`emptyAccum`, `addAccum`, `mergeAccum`, `negateAccum`"
msgstr "`emptyAccum`, `addAccum`, `mergeAccum`, `negateAccum`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:202
msgid "Construct and combine exact sums and differences."
msgstr "正確な和と差を構築し, 結合します."

#: src/algebra/values.md:203
msgid "`signAccum`, `roundAccum`, `exactAccum`"
msgstr "`signAccum`, `roundAccum`, `exactAccum`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:203
msgid ""
"Observe the sign, round once to an amount, or read a finite sum as a "
"`Rational`."
msgstr ""
"符号の観測, 金額への 1 回の丸め, または有限の和の `Rational` としての読み出し"
"を行います."

#: src/algebra/values.md:204
msgid "`splitAccum`"
msgstr "`splitAccum`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:204
msgid ""
"Split a positive exact sum into positive finite amounts with that same exact "
"total. Return `Nothing` for nonpositive or non-finite states, or when the "
"rounded total is infinite."
msgstr ""
"正確な正の和を, 正確な合計が同じになる正の有限な金額に分割します. 正でない状"
"態や非有限の状態, または丸めた合計が無限大になる場合には `Nothing` を返しま"
"す."

#: src/algebra/values.md:205
msgid "`roundRational`"
msgstr "`roundRational`"

#: src/algebra/values.md:205
msgid ""
"Convert a rational using `Nearest` or `ToMultipleOf unit`, returning "
"`Nothing` when the requested conversion is unavailable."
msgstr ""
"`Nearest` または `ToMultipleOf unit` を使って有理数を変換し, 要求された変換が"
"できない場合は `Nothing` を返します."

#: src/algebra/values.md:207
msgid ""
"`isErrorValue` is derived from `valueError`; it is not a method to implement "
"independently. An exact decimal instance returns `Nothing` for "
"`roundRational Nearest` when the rational has no representable exact decimal "
"value. Floating-point instances round to the nearest representable value and "
"do not support `ToMultipleOf`."
msgstr ""
"`isErrorValue` は `valueError` から導出されるので, 独立して実装するメソッドで"
"はありません. 正確な十進数の instance は, 有理数に対して表現可能な正確な十進"
"値がない場合, `roundRational Nearest` に対して `Nothing` を返します. 浮動小数"
"点の instance は最も近い表現可能な値に丸め, `ToMultipleOf` には対応していませ"
"ん."

#: src/algebra/values.md:209
msgid ""
"An accumulator must merge associatively and commutatively with zero as its "
"unit, preserve exact finite sums, and support exact subtraction through "
"negation. Accumulating and rounding a single finite value must preserve that "
"value. `splitAccum` must depend on the total, preserve it exactly, and "
"succeed for every positive finite state with a finite rounded result. If the "
"type represents NaN or infinities, accumulation of those values must follow "
"IEEE addition. Value validation and ties-to-even rounding are also part of "
"the instance contract."
msgstr ""
"アキュムレーターは, ゼロを単位元として結合的かつ可換的に結合でき, 正確な有限"
"和を保持し, 符号反転による正確な減算に対応する必要があります. 単一の有限値を"
"累積して丸めても, その値を保持しなければなりません. `splitAccum` は合計だけに"
"依存し, その合計を正確に保持し, 丸めた結果が有限になるすべての正の有限状態で"
"成功する必要があります. 型が NaN または無限大を表す場合, それらの値の累積は "
"IEEE の加算に従う必要があります. 値の検証と偶数丸めも instance の契約の一部で"
"す."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:3
msgid ""
"The January 10 withdrawal becomes one algebra value containing two terms: a "
"3,000-yen increase in cash and a 3,000-yen decrease in savings deposits. "
"Additional transactions in the same month can be added to this value while "
"retaining their separate amounts."
msgstr ""
"1 月 10 日の引き出しは, 現金の 3,000 円の増加と普通預金の 3,000 円の減少とい"
"う 2 つの項 を含む, 1 つの代数の値になります. 同じ月の他の取引も, それぞれの"
"金額を保持したままこの値に加えられます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:5
msgid ""
"`Alg v b` represents a finite collection of terms with amount type `v` and "
"hat base type `b`. The withdrawal uses `MoneyDecimal` amounts and `HatBase "
"(AccountTitles, Unit)` bases in exchangealgebra-0.6.1.1. The collection "
"corresponds to [Definitions 4 and 5](definitions.md#redundant-algebra-and-"
"linear-combinations); its operations correspond to [Definition 6]"
"(definitions.md#operations)."
msgstr ""
"`Alg v b` は, 金額の型 `v` と Hat 基底の型 `b` を持つ項の有限な集まりを表しま"
"す. 引き出しでは, exchangealgebra-0.6.1.1 の `MoneyDecimal` の金額と "
"`HatBase (AccountTitles, Unit)` の基底を使います. この集まりは[定義 4 と 5]"
"(definitions.md#redundant-algebra-and-linear-combinations)に対応し, その演算"
"は[定義 6](definitions.md#operations)に対応します."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:7
msgid "Construct terms and add them"
msgstr "項を構築して加算する"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:9
msgid ""
"Keep the custom currency declaration so the example is a standalone program. "
"Save the code blocks in their displayed order as `Main.hs`:"
msgstr ""
"例を単独で実行できるプログラムにするため, 独自の通貨の宣言を残してください. "
"コードブロックを表示順に `Main.hs` として保存してください:"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:30
msgid "Attach an amount to each base with `.@`, and add the terms with `.+`:"
msgstr "`.@` で各基底に金額を付け, `.+` で項を加算してください:"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:33 src/exchange/exchange.md:61
#: src/exchange/transfer.md:39 src/journal/journal.md:68
msgid ""
"-- | January 10: withdraw 3,000 yen from Bank A's savings account into "
"cash.\n"
msgstr "-- | 1 月 10 日: A 銀行の普通預金から 3,000 円を現金で引き出します.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:39
msgid ""
"The base with `Not` records the cash increase; the base with `Hat` records "
"the deposit decrease. Both amounts are positive. `norm withdrawal` is 6,000 "
"yen because it counts both terms, even though the cash withdrawn is 3,000 "
"yen. `2 .* withdrawal` doubles each term, without changing its account, "
"currency, or direction."
msgstr ""
"`Not` を持つ基底は現金の増加を記録し, `Hat` を持つ基底は預金の減少を記録しま"
"す. どちらの金額も正です. 引き出した現金は 3,000 円ですが, `norm withdrawal` "
"は両方の項を数えるので 6,000 円です. `2 .* withdrawal` は, 勘定科目, 通貨, 方"
"向を変えずに各項を 2 倍にします."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:41
msgid "Add the month's transactions"
msgstr "月内の取引を加える"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:43
msgid ""
"Suppose the business withdraws another 2,000 yen on January 15, buys goods "
"for 500 yen in cash on January 20, and exchanges 1,500 yen in cash for 10 "
"dollars on January 25. The exchange has no fee and uses 150 yen per dollar. "
"Record each transaction and add it to the month:"
msgstr ""
"事業者が 1 月 15 日にさらに 2,000 円を引き出し, 1 月 20 日に現金 500 円で商品"
"を購入し, 1 月 25 日に現金 1,500 円を 10 ドルに両替するとします. 両替に手数料"
"はなく, 1 ドルを 150 円とします. 各取引を記録し, 月の記録に加えてください:"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:46 src/journal/journal.md:72
msgid "-- | January 15: withdraw another 2,000 yen.\n"
msgstr "-- | 1 月 15 日: さらに 2,000 円を引き出します.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:50
msgid ""
"-- | January 20: buy goods for 500 yen in cash, recorded as Purchases.\n"
msgstr "-- | 1 月 20 日: 現金 500 円で商品を購入し, Purchases に記録します.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:55
msgid ""
"-- | January 25: exchange 1,500 yen in cash for 10 dollars, with no fee.\n"
msgstr "-- | 1 月 25 日: 手数料なしで現金 1,500 円を 10 ドルに両替します.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:60
msgid "-- | Changes recorded during the month, with no opening balances.\n"
msgstr "-- | 期首残高を含まない, 月内に記録された変化です.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:66
msgid ""
"`month` contains the recorded changes without opening balances. Adding the "
"withdrawals with `.+` retains the cash increases of 3,000 and 2,000 as "
"separate amounts on `(Cash, Yen)`. The cash payment and currency exchange "
"also retain separate decreases on that base. No implicit sum or cancellation "
"occurs at a shared base."
msgstr ""
"`month` は期首残高を含まず, 記録された変化を含みます. `.+` で引き出しを加算す"
"ると, `(Cash, Yen)` 上の現金増加 3,000 と 2,000 は別々の金額として保持されま"
"す. 現金払いと両替による減少も, その基底上で別々に保持されます. 同じ基底上で"
"も, 暗黙の合算や相殺は行われません."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:68
msgid ""
"The payment uses `Purchases` for the goods purchased. The exchange reduces "
"yen cash and increases dollar cash; the two currencies remain distinct "
"currency elements. The record omits date and bank account elements from the "
"base because its balances combine dates and do not distinguish bank accounts."
msgstr ""
"支払いでは購入した商品に `Purchases` を使います. 両替は円の現金を減らし, ドル"
"の現金を増やします. 2 つの通貨は別々の要素として保持されます. この記録の残高"
"は日付をまたいで合算し, 銀行口座を区別しないので, 日付と銀行口座の要素は基底"
"に含めません."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:70
msgid "Select an operation"
msgstr "演算を選ぶ"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:72
msgid ""
"**What cash remains in each currency?** Apply `bar` to net the changes "
"within each full base, then `proj` to select Cash without restricting the "
"unit. The yen cash change is 3,000 + 2,000 - 500 - 1,500 = 3,000 yen, and "
"the dollar cash change is 10 dollars. These are balances of the recorded "
"changes; the yen deposit decrease also requires an opening balance to "
"determine the deposit still held."
msgstr ""
"**各通貨の現金はいくら残りますか?** `bar` を適用して完全な基底ごとに変化を相"
"殺し, 次に `proj` で単位を制限せずに Cash を選択してください. 円の現金の変化"
"は 3,000 + 2,000 - 500 - 1,500 = 3,000 円で, ドルの現金の変化は 10 ドルです. "
"これらは記録された変化の残高です. 円の預金の減少についても, 残っている預金を"
"求めるには期首残高が必要です."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:74
msgid ""
"**What is the total of the yen terms?** Select all yen bases with `proj`, "
"then apply `norm`. This measures gross amounts in those terms, counting both "
"directions and both accounts of the withdrawals. It is not a net cash flow. "
"Select a unit before totaling: adding yen and dollar amounts without "
"conversion does not produce a monetary total in either currency."
msgstr ""
"**円の項の合計はいくらですか?** `proj` ですべての円の基底を選択し, 次に "
"`norm` を適用してください. これは記録された金額の総額を測り, 引き出しの両方向"
"と両勘定科目を数えます. 純キャッシュフローではありません. 合計する前に単位を"
"選択してください. 換算せずに円とドルの金額を足しても, どちらの通貨建ての金額"
"の合計としても意味を持ちません."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:76
msgid ""
"**Which cash changes were recorded in yen?** Select `(Cash, Yen)` without "
"applying bar. The original term amounts remain available in the selected "
"algebra."
msgstr ""
"**円で記録された現金の変化はどれですか?** bar を適用せずに `(Cash, Yen)` を選"
"択してください. 選択された代数には, 元の項の金額が保持されます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:79
msgid ""
"-- | Remaining cash by currency after canceling changes within each full "
"base.\n"
msgstr "-- | 完全な基底ごとに変化を相殺した後の, 通貨別の現金残高です.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:82
msgid "-- | Original yen terms on every account and in both directions.\n"
msgstr "-- | すべての勘定科目と両方向にわたる, 元の円の項です.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:86
msgid "-- | Original cash terms in yen, before aggregation.\n"
msgstr "-- | 集約前の, 円建ての現金の項です.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:92
msgid ""
"The query `HatNot :< (Cash, (.#))` restricts the account but leaves "
"direction and currency unrestricted. `HatNot :< ((.#), Yen)` restricts the "
"currency but leaves account and direction unrestricted. A query wildcard "
"matches any stored element. A concrete query element matches only an equal "
"stored element, as in [Query bases by their elements](elements.md#query-"
"elements-and-combine-them-into-bases)."
msgstr ""
"問い合わせ `HatNot :< (Cash, (.#))` は勘定科目を制限し, 方向と通貨は制限しま"
"せん. `HatNot :< ((.#), Yen)` は通貨を制限し, 勘定科目と方向は制限しません. "
"問い合わせのワイルドカードは記録されたどの要素にも一致します. 具体的な要素を"
"指定した問い合わせは, 等しい要素が記録されている場合だけ一致します. [要素を指"
"定して基底を問い合わせる](elements.md#query-elements-and-combine-them-into-"
"bases)を参照してください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:94
msgid ""
"**What are the cash increases and decreases separately?** `compress "
"yenCashPostings` totals each direction independently. It gives an increase "
"total of 5,000 yen and a decrease total of 2,000 yen. `bar` instead cancels "
"the totals and leaves the increase of 3,000 yen. Both operations explicitly "
"discard individual term detail."
msgstr ""
"**現金の増加と減少はそれぞれいくらですか?** `compress yenCashPostings` は各方"
"向を個別に合計します. 増加の合計は 5,000 円, 減少の合計は 2,000 円になりま"
"す. 一方, `bar` は両者の合計を相殺し, 3,000 円の増加を残します. どちらの演算"
"も個々の項の明細を明示的に捨てます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:96
msgid ""
"**What reverses the withdrawal?** `(.^) withdrawal` changes the cash "
"increase into a decrease and the deposit decrease into an increase. Every "
"amount remains 3,000. Adding this value to `withdrawal` keeps both sets of "
"terms; applying `bar` to the sum gives zero. Hat is an involution on "
"direction, not arithmetic negation."
msgstr ""
"**引き出しを逆転させるにはどうしますか?** `(.^) withdrawal` は現金の増加を減"
"少に, 預金の減少を増加に変えます. 各金額は 3,000 のままです. この値を "
"`withdrawal` に加えると, 両方の項の集まりが保持されます. 和に `bar` を適用す"
"るとゼロになります. Hat は方向に関する対合であり, 算術的な符号反転ではありま"
"せん."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:98
msgid "Run the queries"
msgstr "問い合わせを実行する"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:100
msgid "Print each answer with the question or operation that produced it:"
msgstr "各回答を, その回答を得た問い合わせまたは演算とともに表示してください:"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:106
msgid ""
"-- | Print the records and the answers to the cash and currency queries.\n"
msgstr "-- | 記録と, 現金および通貨の問い合わせに対する回答を表示します.\n"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:110
msgid "\"January 10 withdrawal\""
msgstr "\"January 10 withdrawal\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:111
msgid "\"Twice the withdrawal\""
msgstr "\"Twice the withdrawal\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:112
msgid "\"Withdrawal term total in yen\""
msgstr "\"Withdrawal term total in yen\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:113
msgid "\"Yen cash terms before aggregation\""
msgstr "\"Yen cash terms before aggregation\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:114
msgid "\"Cash balances by currency\""
msgstr "\"Cash balances by currency\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:115
msgid "\"Yen terms without cancellation\""
msgstr "\"Yen terms without cancellation\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:116
msgid "\"Yen term total\""
msgstr "\"Yen term total\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:117
msgid "\"Yen cash totals by direction\""
msgstr "\"Yen cash totals by direction\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:118
msgid "\"Yen cash residual amount\""
msgstr "\"Yen cash residual amount\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:119
msgid "\"Reverse the withdrawal directions\""
msgstr "\"Reverse the withdrawal directions\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:120
msgid "\"Withdrawal plus its hat, before bar\""
msgstr "\"Withdrawal plus its hat, before bar\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:121
msgid "\"Withdrawal plus its hat, after bar\""
msgstr "\"Withdrawal plus its hat, after bar\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:141
msgid ""
"`Yen cash terms before aggregation` retains the separate withdrawal and "
"payment amounts. `Cash balances by currency` contains the net cash changes "
"in yen and dollars, while `Yen term total` counts the gross yen amounts on "
"every account. `Yen cash totals by direction` contains the separate increase "
"and decrease totals. The named withdrawal-plus-hat results distinguish "
"retaining opposing terms from canceling them with bar."
msgstr ""
"`Yen cash terms before aggregation` は, 引き出しと支払いの金額を別々に保持し"
"ています. `Cash balances by currency` は円とドルの現金の純変化を含み, `Yen "
"term total` はすべての勘定科目にわたる円金額の総額を数えます. `Yen cash "
"totals by direction` は増加と減少の合計を別々に含みます. 引き出しとその hat "
"の和の名前付きの結果では, 逆方向の項を保持する場合と, bar で相殺する場合を区"
"別しています."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:143
msgid ""
"The displayed sequence order can differ from the source expression's order. "
"Construction routes can arrange the same terms differently, and structural "
"`Eq` can observe that arrangement. Do not infer chronological order from the "
"printed algebra. When comparing aggregated content, choose an explicit "
"`compress` or `bar` according to whether the opposing directions must remain "
"separate."
msgstr ""
"表示される列の順序は, 元の式の順序と異なる場合があります. 構築経路によって同"
"じ項の並び方が変わり, 構造的な `Eq` はその並び方を区別できます. 表示された代"
"数から時系列の順序を推測しないでください. 集約した内容を比較するときは, 逆方"
"向を別々に保持する必要があるかに応じて, `compress` または `bar` を明示的に選"
"んでください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:149
msgid "Construction and operations"
msgstr "構築と演算"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:151
msgid ""
"`Alg` requires a `HatVal` amount type and a `HatBaseClass` base type. Its "
"`Redundant` instance implements the operations; defining a new element type "
"does not require another `Redundant` instance. `Zero` is the empty algebra "
"and the identity for addition. For value and direction checks, see "
"[Construction and scalar checks](values.md#construction-and-scalar-checks)."
msgstr ""
"`Alg` は金額の型に `HatVal` を, 基底の型に `HatBaseClass` を要求します. その "
"`Redundant` の instance が演算を実装します. 新しい要素の型を定義しても, 別の "
"`Redundant` の instance は不要です. `Zero` は空の代数であり, 加算の単位元で"
"す. 値と方向の検査については, [構築時とスカラーの検査]"
"(values.md#construction-and-scalar-checks)を参照してください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:153
msgid ""
"The public `(:@)` pattern matches a singleton term but cannot construct one "
"in 0.6.1.1. Construct terms with `.@`. `toList` returns singleton terms, "
"`vals` returns amounts, and `bases` returns hat bases."
msgstr ""
"公開パターン `(:@)` は単一の項に一致しますが, 0.6.1.1 では項を構築できませ"
"ん. 項は `.@` で構築してください. `toList` は単一の項を並べたリストを, "
"`vals` は金額を, `bases` は Hat 基底を返します."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:155 src/exchange/exchange.md:122
#: src/exchange/transfer.md:121 src/journal/journal.md:181
#: src/journal/agents.md:138 src/bookkeeping/admission.md:174
#: src/bookkeeping/trial-balance.md:238 src/bookkeeping/adjustment.md:247
#: src/bookkeeping/closing.md:265 src/bookkeeping/statements.md:293
#: src/bookkeeping/consolidation.md:323 src/io/input.md:148
#: src/io/output.md:369
msgid "Inputs and result"
msgstr "入力と結果"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:157
msgid "`x .+ y`"
msgstr "`x .+ y`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:157
msgid ""
"Retain the terms from both algebras. Equal bases do not cause immediate "
"summation or cancellation. `(<>)` is the same addition."
msgstr ""
"両方の代数の項を保持します. 基底が等しくても, 即座の合算や相殺は行いません. "
"`(<>)` も同じ加算です."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:158
msgid "`scalar .* x`"
msgstr "`scalar .* x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:158
msgid ""
"Multiply every amount by the scalar, preserving the term structure except "
"for zero products. See the input checks in [Values](values.md#construction-"
"and-scalar-checks)."
msgstr ""
"各金額をスカラー倍し, 積がゼロになる場合を除いて項の構造を保持します. [値]"
"(values.md#construction-and-scalar-checks)の入力検査を参照してください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:159
msgid "`norm x`"
msgstr "`norm x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:159
msgid ""
"Total all stored amounts on both directions. Return an amount, losing base "
"and direction information."
msgstr ""
"両方向に記録されたすべての金額を合計します. 金額を返し, 基底と方向の情報は失"
"われます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:160
msgid "`bar x`, also written `(.-) x`"
msgstr "`bar x` または `(.-) x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:160
msgid ""
"Total the opposing directions at each full base and keep only the excess on "
"the winning direction. Remove an exactly canceled base."
msgstr ""
"完全な基底ごとに逆方向の金額を合計し, 大きい方向の超過分だけを残します. 完全"
"に相殺された基底を取り除きます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:161
msgid "`compress x`"
msgstr "`compress x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:161
msgid ""
"Total each direction at each full base separately, without cancellation. "
"This explicitly discards the separate terms within each direction."
msgstr ""
"完全な基底ごとに各方向を別々に合計し, 相殺しません. 各方向の個々の項は明示的"
"に捨てます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:162
msgid "`(.^) x`"
msgstr "`(.^) x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:162
msgid "Swap `Hat` and `Not` for every term, preserving each amount."
msgstr "各金額を保持し, すべての項の `Hat` と `Not` を入れ替えます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:163
msgid "`proj patterns x`"
msgstr "`proj patterns x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:163
msgid ""
"Select terms whose hat bases match at least one query pattern, without "
"netting or changing amounts."
msgstr ""
"Hat 基底が少なくとも 1 つの問い合わせパターンに一致する項を選択し, 相殺や金額"
"の変更は行いません."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:164
msgid "`projNetNorm patterns x`"
msgstr "`projNetNorm patterns x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:164
msgid ""
"Select bases, net within each full base, total the magnitudes of the "
"residuals, and round once. Return an amount."
msgstr ""
"基底を選択し, 完全な基底ごとに相殺し, 残差の大きさを合計して 1 回だけ丸めま"
"す. 金額を返します."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:166
msgid ""
"In 0.6.1.1, `.*` has the default fixity `infixl 9`, and `.+` is `infixr 3`. "
"Parenthesize mixed expressions to state the intended grouping, such as "
"`(2 .* withdrawal) .+ cashPayment`."
msgstr ""
"0.6.1.1 では, `.*` の結合性と優先順位は既定の `infixl 9` で, `.+` は `infixr "
"3` です. 演算を混ぜた式は, `(2 .* withdrawal) .+ cashPayment` のように括弧で"
"意図したまとまりを示してください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:168
msgid "Projections and rounding"
msgstr "射影と丸め"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:170
msgid ""
"Overlapping or repeated `proj` patterns select each term once. "
"`projByAccountTitle` from `ExchangeAlgebra.Accounting.Exchange`, also re-"
"exported by `ExchangeAlgebra`, selects an account regardless of the other "
"elements of the base."
msgstr ""
"`proj` のパターンが重複していても, 各項は 1 回だけ選択されます. "
"`ExchangeAlgebra.Accounting.Exchange` の `projByAccountTitle` は, "
"`ExchangeAlgebra` からも再エクスポートされており, 基底の他の要素にかかわらず"
"勘定科目を選択します."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:172
msgid ""
"`bar` and `projNetNorm` net within each full base; yen and dollar cash "
"cannot cancel each other. For exact decimal amounts, `projNetNorm patterns "
"x` agrees with `norm (bar (proj patterns x))`. Floating-point results can "
"differ because the latter expression rounds each base's residual before "
"summing."
msgstr ""
"`bar` と `projNetNorm` は完全な基底ごとに相殺するので, 円とドルの現金は互いに"
"相殺できません. 正確な十進数の金額では, `projNetNorm patterns x` は `norm "
"(bar (proj patterns x))` と一致します. 浮動小数点の結果は, 後者の式が合計の前"
"に各基底の残差を丸めるため, 異なる場合があります."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:174
msgid ""
"**Caution:** `compress` discards separate term amounts, and floating-point "
"rounding of the direction totals can change the result of a later `bar`. "
"Preserve the original algebra when individual terms are needed."
msgstr ""
"**注意:** `compress` は個々の項の金額を捨てます. また, 方向別の合計に対する浮"
"動小数点の丸めにより, その後の `bar` の結果が変わる場合があります. 個々の項が"
"必要な場合は, 元の代数を保持してください."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:3
msgid ""
"The January 10 withdrawal has a debit of 3,000 yen to Cash and a credit of "
"3,000 yen to Deposits. An exchange algebra is a redundant algebra with "
"account classifications on its bases and decompositions into debit and "
"credit terms. The classifications correspond to [Definition 7](../algebra/"
"definitions.md#account-classes-and-sides), and the decompositions correspond "
"to [Definition 8](../algebra/definitions.md#debit-and-credit-decomposition)."
msgstr ""
"1 月 10 日の引き出しでは, 借方に現金 3,000 円, 貸方に預金 3,000 円を記録しま"
"す. 交換代数は, 基底に勘定科目の区分を持ち, 項を借方と貸方に分解できる冗長代"
"数です. 区分は[定義 7](../algebra/definitions.md#account-classes-and-sides), "
"分解は[定義 8](../algebra/definitions.md#debit-and-credit-decomposition)に対"
"応します."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:5
msgid ""
"Use exchangealgebra-0.6.1.1 in the project prepared in [Add the package to a "
"Stack project](../usage/installation.md#add-the-package-to-a-stack-project). "
"The example keeps the custom `Unit` and the account-and-unit base from [The "
"redundant algebra](../algebra/redundant.md). It adds an instance for account "
"access, then checks the withdrawal's sides and balance."
msgstr ""
"[Stack プロジェクトにパッケージを追加する](../usage/installation.md#add-the-"
"package-to-a-stack-project)に従い, exchangealgebra-0.6.1.1 を使ってください. "
"例では[冗長代数](../algebra/redundant.md)で使った自作の `Unit` と勘定科目と単"
"位の基底を保ちます. 勘定科目へアクセスする instance を加えて, 引き出しの貸借"
"の側と均衡を確かめます."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:7
